RED phase: Main factory function that ties L1+L2+L3 together

## Factory function
```typescript
export function createFastRegistry(
  targetNamespace: DurableObjectNamespace,
  config?: FastRegistryConfig & {
    indexDO?: DurableObjectNamespace  // Optional L2
  }
): FastRegistry

interface FastRegistry {
  // Get stub by name - uses L1→L2→L3 lookup
  getStub(name: string, ctx?: ExecutionContext): Promise<DurableObjectStub>

  // Get stub with detailed result
  getStubWithResult(name: string, ctx?: ExecutionContext): Promise<{
    stub: DurableObjectStub
    entry: FastRegistryEntry
    tier: 'l1-cache' | 'l2-index' | 'l3-created'
    latencyMs: number
  }>

  // Register a new entry (called after L3 creation)
  register(entry: FastRegistryEntry): Promise<void>

  // Invalidate cache
  invalidate(name: string): Promise<void>

  // Get stats
  getStats(): FastRegistryStats
}
```

## Key behavior
- L1 hit: return cached entry, use idFromString(hexId)
- L2 hit: return indexed entry, cache it, use idFromString(hexId)  
- L3 fallback: newUniqueId(), register in background, return stub

## Test cases
- getStub returns stub from L1 cache
- getStub falls back to L2 on cache miss
- getStub creates new DO on L2 miss
- New DO is registered in background
- Stats track hits/misses correctly

RED phase: Implement L2 Index DO for persistent storage

## Architecture
L2 Index DO stores name→hexId mappings in SQLite for fast regional lookups.

## FastRegistryDO class
```typescript
export class FastRegistryDO implements DurableObject {
  // SQLite schema
  // CREATE TABLE entries (
  //   namespace TEXT,
  //   name TEXT,
  //   hex_id TEXT,
  //   location_hint TEXT,
  //   created_at INTEGER,
  //   last_accessed_at INTEGER,
  //   metadata TEXT,
  //   PRIMARY KEY (namespace, name)
  // )

  // Endpoints
  // GET /lookup/{namespace}/{name} → FastRegistryEntry | 404
  // POST /register → { ok: true }
  // POST /access → { ok: true } (update lastAccessedAt)
  // GET /stats → { totalEntries, byNamespace }
}
```

## Test cases
- Lookup returns entry if exists
- Lookup returns 404 if not found
- Register creates new entry
- Register updates existing entry (upsert)
- Access updates lastAccessedAt
- Stats returns correct counts
